    <item>
        <title>This site, so far</title>
        <link>https://follo.eth.sucks/2DD17D5A-DFEF-4F7D-A8C8-039AA3AB8DE9/</link>
        <guid>https://follo.eth.sucks/2DD17D5A-DFEF-4F7D-A8C8-039AA3AB8DE9/</guid>
        <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 16:26:50 -0300</pubDate>
        
        <itunes:image href="https://k51qzi5uqu5dilqjwgdm3zj0g24zaowqfxoargdm1lbj7s4frpwuzqp2tmxm4g.eth.sucks/2DD17D5A-DFEF-4F7D-A8C8-039AA3AB8DE9/_cover.png" />    
        
        
        <description><![CDATA[
            <p>A widget can read the whole site it lives in. This one draws every post on this site as a timeline, straight from <code>planet.json</code>, and updates itself every time the site is published.</p>
<div id="timeline" style="border:1px solid var(--foreground-secondary-color);padding:16px">loading…</div>
<p style="font-size:13px;opacity:.6">How: twenty lines inline in the post, using <code>croptop.site()</code>. The same call can build an archive page, a tag cloud, or "you might also like".</p>
<script type="module">
croptop.ready(({ site }) => {
  const el = document.getElementById("timeline");
  const posts = [...site.articles].sort((a, b) => a.created - b.created);
  const toDate = (t) => new Date((t + 978307200) * 1000);
  const first = toDate(posts[0].created), last = toDate(posts[posts.length - 1].created);
  const span = Math.max(1, last - first);
  el.innerHTML = `<div style="font-size:13px;opacity:.7">${posts.length} posts between ${first.toLocaleDateString()} and ${last.toLocaleDateString()}</div>
    <div style="position:relative;height:56px;margin:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--foreground-secondary-color)"></div><ol style="margin:0;padding-left:18px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7"></ol>`;
  const track = el.children[1], list = el.children[2];
  posts.forEach((p) => {
    const x = (toDate(p.created) - first) / span * 100;
    const dot = document.createElement("a"); dot.href = croptop.prefix + p.id + "/"; dot.title = p.title || "untitled";
    dot.style.cssText = `position:absolute;left:calc(${x}% - 6px);bottom:-6px;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:${p.id === croptop.postId ? "#3bb273" : "var(--link-color)"}`;
    track.appendChild(dot);
    const li = document.createElement("li"); li.innerHTML = `<a href="${croptop.prefix}${p.id}/">${p.title || "untitled"}</a> <span style="opacity:.5">${toDate(p.created).toLocaleDateString()}</span>`;
    list.appendChild(li);
  });
});
</script>

        ]]></description>
    </item>
    
    <item>
        <title>Who is reading this</title>
        <link>https://follo.eth.sucks/D4917B9F-6155-49FF-B9BF-F5CC584C8393/</link>
        <guid>https://follo.eth.sucks/D4917B9F-6155-49FF-B9BF-F5CC584C8393/</guid>
        <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 16:26:50 -0300</pubDate>
        
        <itunes:image href="https://k51qzi5uqu5dilqjwgdm3zj0g24zaowqfxoargdm1lbj7s4frpwuzqp2tmxm4g.eth.sucks/D4917B9F-6155-49FF-B9BF-F5CC584C8393/_cover.png" />    
        
        
        <description><![CDATA[
            <p>Posts can talk to the reader's wallet. This one asks who you are and shows you your own balance, read-only. Nothing is signed, nothing is sent, nothing leaves your browser.</p>
<div style="border:1px solid var(--foreground-secondary-color);padding:16px">
  <button id="wallet-connect" style="font:inherit;padding:8px 14px;cursor:pointer">Connect wallet</button>
  <div id="wallet-card" hidden>
    <div style="font-size:12px;opacity:.6">you</div><div id="wallet-address" style="font-size:20px">…</div>
    <div id="wallet-balance" style="opacity:.8;margin:6px 0 12px">…</div>
    <button id="wallet-pledge-btn" style="font:inherit;padding:8px 14px;cursor:pointer">Pledge to follow the money</button>
    <div id="wallet-pledge" style="font-size:13px;margin-top:8px"></div>
  </div>
  <div id="wallet-note" style="font-size:13px;opacity:.7;margin-top:8px"></div>
</div>
<p style="font-size:13px;opacity:.6">How: <code>wallet.js</code> attached to this post, using <code>croptop.wallet.connect()</code> and a public RPC. The buy button on every post uses the same plumbing to send real transactions.</p>
<script type="module" src="wallet.js"></script>

        ]]></description>
